WEBVTT

00:00:10.150 --> 00:00:19.800
<b>LEGEND</b>

00:00:10.150 --> 00:00:19.800
<b>OF THE</b>

00:00:10.150 --> 00:00:19.800
<b>  GALACTIC HEROES</b>

00:02:04.410 --> 00:02:07.930
They say you need to investigate
the crime scene a hundred times.

00:02:07.930 --> 00:02:13.510
It is the most basic move to go back to the crime scene when the investigation reaches a stalemate.

00:02:13.510 --> 00:02:15.600
Is there something
that's bothering you ?

00:02:17.040 --> 00:02:20.350
No, it's nothing
in particular.

00:02:20.350 --> 00:02:23.240
It's just that I can't think
of anything else to do.

00:02:30.140 --> 00:02:34.400
Dreams of the Morning, Songs of the Night

00:02:30.140 --> 00:02:34.400
Chapter 4

00:03:28.700 --> 00:03:30.600
This is the
murder weapon, Kircheis.

00:03:31.550 --> 00:03:37.430
Drop a 30 kilogram bag of wheat on someone's head from a height of 15 meters...

00:03:37.430 --> 00:03:39.560
...and it will crush their skull,
causing immediate death.

00:03:39.560 --> 00:03:43.500
After that, it gets cleaned
up by the dust collector.

00:03:43.500 --> 00:03:46.500
If you fold the bag
and take it with you...

00:03:46.500 --> 00:03:50.350
...then there is no murder weapon left
and a perfect murder can be committed.

00:03:53.400 --> 00:03:56.050
We should have known without
witnessing such a happening.

00:03:57.090 --> 00:04:02.300
No, because it was him, he was able to figure it out right here and now.

00:04:03.320 --> 00:04:07.500
But there's one big hole
in this inference, Kircheis.

00:04:08.200 --> 00:04:10.150
What do you mean ?

00:04:10.150 --> 00:04:13.320
Why didn't the perpetrator
make it look like an accident ?

00:04:14.600 --> 00:04:19.930
If he had left the bag and left the entrance open people would have thought it was an accident.

00:04:20.740 --> 00:04:22.140
I see.

00:04:22.140 --> 00:04:25.000
The school would be held responsible for its
lack of control, but that would be about it.

00:04:27.600 --> 00:04:28.590
What's wrong ?

00:04:33.580 --> 00:04:34.580
I see.

00:04:34.580 --> 00:04:35.930
That's what is going on.

00:04:36.930 --> 00:04:38.040
Kircheis.

00:04:38.040 --> 00:04:39.700
There's something I want
you to check on immediately.

00:04:53.790 --> 00:04:54.810
Lord Reinhard.

00:04:55.510 --> 00:04:56.520
Please look at this.

00:04:58.400 --> 00:04:59.650
Just as I thought.

00:05:10.290 --> 00:05:13.590
The first victim,
Karl von Reifeisen...

00:05:13.590 --> 00:05:17.590
...probably found out that the perpetrator
is colorblind and threatened him.

00:05:17.590 --> 00:05:23.880
He demanded something, and this stirred
up a defensive motive in the perpetrator.

00:05:24.990 --> 00:05:31.900
The second victim witnessed the first murder
and caused the perpetrator to lose control.

00:05:33.840 --> 00:05:34.840
I see.

00:05:34.840 --> 00:05:37.730
That makes sense.

00:05:37.730 --> 00:05:38.680
So, who is the perpetrator ?

00:05:39.420 --> 00:05:42.300
I will show you now...

00:05:42.300 --> 00:05:43.700
...by using this.

00:05:48.340 --> 00:05:49.410
Come in.

00:06:03.720 --> 00:06:06.590
What is it, Captain Musel ?

00:06:07.810 --> 00:06:10.100
Read this sentence, Haase.

00:06:10.500 --> 00:06:12.800
Haase is the perpetrator.

00:06:38.110 --> 00:06:39.710
What's wrong, Haase ?

00:06:39.710 --> 00:06:41.700
It's not that you
can't read, is it ?

00:06:57.200 --> 00:06:58.590
Or is it you
can't read that ?

00:07:01.880 --> 00:07:03.560
No, Captain !

00:07:03.560 --> 00:07:04.950
I can't read it !

00:07:07.990 --> 00:07:10.730
I'm colorblind.

00:07:10.730 --> 00:07:12.280
Severely.

00:07:12.980 --> 00:07:15.240
I admit it !

00:07:15.240 --> 00:07:19.310
So please drop your act !

00:07:24.120 --> 00:07:26.210
Is that your
true personality ?

00:07:26.210 --> 00:07:30.200
You're quiet on the surface, but because
of that your emotions build up inside.

00:07:33.260 --> 00:07:34.200
Haase...

00:07:34.200 --> 00:07:36.150
...I'm disappointed.

00:07:36.150 --> 00:07:37.690
Really disappointed.

00:07:39.170 --> 00:07:41.130
Although you have your reasons...

00:07:41.130 --> 00:07:47.150
...I'm disappointed that an excellent student like yourself killed a fellow student.

00:07:48.480 --> 00:07:51.880
I can't help but
feel sorry for myself.

00:07:54.230 --> 00:07:57.470
Haase is not the
perpetrator, Principal.

00:07:58.280 --> 00:07:59.040
What ?

00:07:59.040 --> 00:08:01.100
But you just said...

00:08:01.100 --> 00:08:03.800
The only thing I'm holding
Haase responsible for...

00:08:03.800 --> 00:08:08.350
...is that he lied about his
colorblindness to enter military school.

00:08:08.350 --> 00:08:10.930
The real perpetrator
is someone else.

00:08:26.950 --> 00:08:29.010
This is the knife
that killed Bertz.

00:08:29.800 --> 00:08:34.780
This was found in Erich von
Warburg's room a minute ago.

00:08:37.030 --> 00:08:40.920
He was arrested by the
other military policemen.

00:08:40.920 --> 00:08:44.200
It's not official,
but we got his confession.

00:08:44.200 --> 00:08:47.860
He confessed that he
murdered Reifeisen and Bertz.

00:08:48.410 --> 00:08:50.880
No, that can't be !

00:08:50.880 --> 00:08:52.700
He's not the perpetrator !

00:08:52.700 --> 00:08:56.590
That knife was in the
drawer of Haase's desk !

00:09:01.270 --> 00:09:03.800
That is correct, sir.

00:09:03.800 --> 00:09:08.690
But how did you know
that fact, Principal Steger ?

00:09:21.160 --> 00:09:23.210
Haase is at the
top of the class.

00:09:23.210 --> 00:09:25.280
The late Bertz
was in second.

00:09:26.320 --> 00:09:32.740
If those two disappear, the third in the class
will automatically become the top of the class.

00:09:32.740 --> 00:09:36.700
The name of the student who is third
in the class is Erich von Warburg.

00:09:36.700 --> 00:09:39.200
His last name is not
important for this mystery.

00:09:39.820 --> 00:09:43.350
What is important is the last name of
his grandfather on his mother's side.

00:09:45.800 --> 00:09:47.270
Steger.

00:09:47.270 --> 00:09:50.680
Gearhard von Steger
is his grandfather's name.

00:09:56.370 --> 00:09:58.160
Captain Musel.

00:09:58.160 --> 00:10:02.550
I always thought you had a questionable
sense of humor when you were in school...

00:10:02.550 --> 00:10:05.820
...but you haven't
improved a bit since then.

00:10:05.820 --> 00:10:07.550
Actually, it's getting worse.

00:10:08.030 --> 00:10:09.740
I want you to retract that.

00:10:09.740 --> 00:10:14.180
It's a bad truth,
not a bad joke.

00:10:14.800 --> 00:10:19.040
At any rate,
I will continue to speak.

00:10:19.040 --> 00:10:20.880
I'm not finished yet.

00:10:23.340 --> 00:10:28.590
The first incident, the death of Karl von Reifeisen, was an unfortunate accident.

00:10:30.680 --> 00:10:35.070
He thought that the reason why
the cafeteria food was so meager...

00:10:35.070 --> 00:10:39.730
...was that the people working in the cafeteria
were selling foodstuffs on the black market.

00:10:40.790 --> 00:10:45.150
So he secretly entered
the food warehouse.

00:10:48.030 --> 00:10:53.750
He not only did it for justice, but he probably did it since, if he found evidence of fraud...

00:10:53.750 --> 00:10:56.600
...he'd get a positive evaluation
from the military academy.

00:11:01.750 --> 00:11:04.700
And Reifeisen had an
unfortunate accident.

00:11:13.280 --> 00:11:19.450
You discovered it during your patrol
that night, and you were in a dilemma.

00:11:20.580 --> 00:11:24.550
You'd be questioned for your lack of
management as a principal for sure.

00:11:24.550 --> 00:11:27.560
But you came up with an idea
to kill two birds with one stone.

00:11:32.490 --> 00:11:37.460
You emptied the wheat bag
and threw it away.

00:11:39.090 --> 00:11:44.100
You locked the door from the
outside to make it a murder.

00:11:44.750 --> 00:11:47.550
If it was an accident, you would be
responsible for lack of management...

00:11:47.550 --> 00:11:51.130
...but if it was a murder, the perpetrator
will be responsible for everything.

00:11:56.650 --> 00:12:00.950
I don't know if you planned to make
Haase the perpetrator from the beginning.

00:12:00.950 --> 00:12:05.300
You seemed to know that
Haase was colorblind...

00:12:05.300 --> 00:12:08.850
...so you could have expelled
him by announcing that fact.

00:12:10.050 --> 00:12:12.750
But even if you got rid of Haase,
who is at the top of the class...

00:12:12.750 --> 00:12:15.300
...there was still Bertz, who was the second
in the class, before your grandson.

00:12:15.300 --> 00:12:22.900
So by killing Bertz and putting the blame
on Haase, you'd get rid of both of them.

00:12:22.900 --> 00:12:26.700
You killed Bertz for
your beloved grandson.

00:12:28.570 --> 00:12:35.940
Your downfall is the fact that the military
police sent an inexperienced person.

00:12:35.940 --> 00:12:40.400
You took great trouble to make it
look like Haase was the perpetrator.

00:12:41.710 --> 00:12:48.650
You sent Haase to the soccer ground
and used the green tile as a prop.

00:12:50.300 --> 00:12:54.320
I'm sorry to trouble you
{respectable teacher} even after we graduated.

00:12:57.640 --> 00:12:59.060
Drop your useless resistance.

00:13:08.320 --> 00:13:13.860
Kircheis won the gold medal many times
for shooting while he was in school.

00:13:14.680 --> 00:13:17.250
You won't even
have a chance to fire.

00:13:28.990 --> 00:13:31.100
You are a coward.

00:13:31.640 --> 00:13:36.500
You only think of your position,
and you used that position...

00:13:36.500 --> 00:13:39.220
...to set a trap for the others to
satisfy your beloved grandson's ego.

00:13:40.580 --> 00:13:44.150
Bertz, who was killed, probably
has a grandfather, too.

00:13:45.400 --> 00:13:50.070
Compared to you, the fugitives who ran
away to the so called Free Planets Alliance...

00:13:50.070 --> 00:13:53.470
...have much more
integrity than you.

00:13:53.470 --> 00:13:57.920
At least they know that in order for them to
get something, they need to lose something.

00:13:57.920 --> 00:14:01.630
Their country, for example.

00:14:03.120 --> 00:14:09.900
What you should be hating is the superiority
that would expel a top student like Haase...

00:14:09.900 --> 00:14:16.020
...because he's colorblind, even though it has
nothing to do with the ability of the individual.

00:14:16.790 --> 00:14:20.690
Why do you not defy your
superiors, but go after the weak ?

00:14:21.070 --> 00:14:23.910
You will never understand.

00:14:25.960 --> 00:14:29.010
A person like you who advanced
to captain at the age of 17...

00:14:29.010 --> 00:14:34.140
...just because your sister is loved by the
Kaiser will never understand my problems.

00:14:36.130 --> 00:14:37.570
You say it's unjust ?

00:14:37.570 --> 00:14:41.650
Do you think I was
never treated unjustly ?

00:14:41.650 --> 00:14:45.260
Why do you think I knew about
Haase's colorblindness to begin with ?

00:14:47.930 --> 00:14:49.850
Haase's grandfather told me !

00:14:51.040 --> 00:14:54.610
His grandfather
was my superior.

00:14:54.610 --> 00:14:58.970
I was told this by my superior and
was forced to be an accomplice.

00:14:58.970 --> 00:15:00.200
Without having a choice.

00:15:03.100 --> 00:15:05.950
I didn't even have
the choice to refuse.

00:15:05.950 --> 00:15:08.350
I endured the injustice
from my superior !

00:15:08.350 --> 00:15:09.450
From the military !

00:15:09.450 --> 00:15:11.210
From society !

00:15:11.210 --> 00:15:13.480
And I've finally gotten here !

00:15:13.480 --> 00:15:14.410
You will never understand !

00:15:15.040 --> 00:15:17.660
I set my dreams on
my daughter's husband.

00:15:17.660 --> 00:15:20.000
But he was
killed in the war.

00:15:20.000 --> 00:15:22.770
I transferred my dreams from
the husband to my grandson...

00:15:22.770 --> 00:15:24.990
...and got rid of
any obstacles for him !

00:15:24.990 --> 00:15:26.590
What's wrong with that ?!

00:15:33.640 --> 00:15:36.960
If there were anyone who had
the right to hate Lord Reinhard...

00:15:36.960 --> 00:15:41.860
...it might not be the nobility
that holds power in this society.

00:15:42.950 --> 00:15:46.880
People like Steger who wish for small
successes and small reformations...

00:15:46.880 --> 00:15:53.900
...within the rules of society are the
ones who see Lord Reinhard as an enemy.

00:15:54.830 --> 00:15:59.420
The reason why Lord Reinhard does not
get angry is because he understands that.

00:16:01.030 --> 00:16:06.450
You should make Bertz's family
understand your reasons first.

00:16:07.610 --> 00:16:10.160
I have nothing
more to say.

00:16:54.410 --> 00:16:55.580
Lord Reinhard.

00:16:57.500 --> 00:17:03.230
Haase's colorblindness will appear
in Principal Steger's confession.

00:17:03.230 --> 00:17:04.770
It's not something we can hide.

00:17:06.720 --> 00:17:10.320
I will make a plea to
lessen his punishment.

00:17:11.220 --> 00:17:14.550
This means that the military
school lost a principal...

00:17:14.550 --> 00:17:18.650
...and the top three students
in the school at the same time.

00:17:19.660 --> 00:17:20.860
Three ?

00:17:21.740 --> 00:17:26.300
Warburg will be expelled
along with Principal Steger.

00:17:26.300 --> 00:17:29.200
Even if not, he won't be
able to stay in this school.

00:17:30.370 --> 00:17:30.890
I see.

00:17:31.880 --> 00:17:32.990
You're right.

00:18:10.840 --> 00:18:11.650
Did you hear ?

00:18:11.650 --> 00:18:15.350
Haase is severely colorblind.

00:18:15.350 --> 00:18:17.250
What nerve he had.

00:18:17.250 --> 00:18:20.220
He hid his genetic defect
to enter military school.

00:18:20.220 --> 00:18:24.350
It's our shame that he
was the top of the class.

00:18:24.350 --> 00:18:26.440
All of his records
will be erased anyway.

00:18:26.440 --> 00:18:29.320
I didn't like
him to start with.

00:18:29.320 --> 00:18:30.330
Yeah.

00:18:30.330 --> 00:18:32.250
He was a weird guy.

00:18:32.250 --> 00:18:33.890
He was a shrewd guy.

00:18:34.470 --> 00:18:35.510
Stop it !

00:18:39.100 --> 00:18:44.600
Just because Haase is colorblind,
is that a reason to be disdainful of him ?!

00:18:44.600 --> 00:18:48.820
Is it the individual's fault that
one has a genetic defect ?!

00:18:49.700 --> 00:18:53.540
Regardless, he was
at the top of the class !

00:18:54.250 --> 00:18:57.080
That was due to
his own efforts !

00:18:57.080 --> 00:19:00.190
None of you were
able to match him !

00:19:02.940 --> 00:19:06.960
Even so, you think you have the
right to discriminate against him ?!

00:19:53.680 --> 00:19:55.980
Must people discriminate
against others ?

00:19:57.120 --> 00:19:59.630
People discriminate
against weaker people.

00:19:59.630 --> 00:20:02.250
No, just because
others are different...

00:20:02.250 --> 00:20:07.000
...people discriminate and attack
others to satisfy their self-esteem.

00:20:08.200 --> 00:20:14.390
And they don't realize that discrimination
is embedded in the system.

00:20:15.370 --> 00:20:19.260
Lord Reinhard always
looks up to fly...

00:20:19.260 --> 00:20:23.550
...but what if people's real nature
is to crawl around the earth...

00:20:23.550 --> 00:20:27.750
...and devour each other in the same
environment to search for happiness ?

00:20:35.150 --> 00:20:40.100
Do you disdain those with
small dreams, Lord Reinhard ?

00:20:44.210 --> 00:20:46.660
I don't care about
the size of the dreams...

00:20:46.660 --> 00:20:49.200
...but I have no
respect for the weak...

00:20:49.200 --> 00:20:52.720
...no, the ones who
settle for being weak.

00:20:54.140 --> 00:20:56.820
Those who don't insist on
their rights act as accomplices...

00:20:56.820 --> 00:21:01.300
...when the rights of others
are being taken away.

00:21:01.770 --> 00:21:05.100
There is no way I can
like those people.

00:21:06.350 --> 00:21:08.660
You think the same way,
don't you, Kircheis ?

00:21:09.860 --> 00:21:13.530
You will always feel
the same way I do, right ?

00:21:15.920 --> 00:21:17.750
Yes, Lord Reinhard.

00:21:22.810 --> 00:21:28.190
The answer was different
from what Kircheis wanted...

00:21:28.190 --> 00:21:32.290
...but Kircheis felt
that he received more.

00:21:34.640 --> 00:21:39.810
He was able to share his
dream with this blond angel.

00:21:41.220 --> 00:21:49.460
It was foolish of him to worry that Reinhard would scoff at his small dream to be beside him always.

00:21:50.410 --> 00:21:53.740
It's impossible for a shadow
to separate from the body.

00:22:18.940 --> 00:22:23.260
This might have been a
dream of early summer.

00:22:24.310 --> 00:22:27.430
How long can
they dream this ?

00:22:27.430 --> 00:22:30.570
Or is there an
end to this dream ?

00:22:30.570 --> 00:22:33.210
These two, at that time,
didn't even think about it.

00:22:43.700 --> 00:22:55.980
I don't wait to live a life of counting memories

00:22:43.910 --> 00:22:49.550
[ Long Relationship ]

00:22:43.910 --> 00:22:49.550
Ending Theme

00:22:43.910 --> 00:22:49.550
Vocals: Ogura Kei

00:22:50.660 --> 00:22:56.290
Reinhard:

00:22:50.660 --> 00:22:56.290
Horikawa Ryo

00:22:57.350 --> 00:23:10.400
But with you, I've had a long relationship...

00:22:57.400 --> 00:23:03.100
Steger:

00:22:57.400 --> 00:23:03.100
Fujimoto Yuzuru

00:23:11.850 --> 00:23:17.200
...and it feels as though the memories...

00:23:11.940 --> 00:23:17.560
Narrator:

00:23:11.940 --> 00:23:17.560
Yara Yuusaku

00:23:18.150 --> 00:23:24.770
...might get carried off somewhere

00:23:19.250 --> 00:23:24.240
Translation:
Toshiaki

00:23:24.240 --> 00:23:30.240
Timing:
Todd Perkins

00:23:24.770 --> 00:23:31.350
Maybe it's a momentary worry

00:23:30.240 --> 00:23:36.250
Song Translation:
Toshiaki

00:23:32.050 --> 00:23:38.050
Thinking, "People change," I shake my head

00:23:36.250 --> 00:23:42.450
Editing:
Todd Perkins
Barbara
Dave
Brain
Mouse
Steve S.
Horus

00:23:38.750 --> 00:23:48.400
The sunset sky and the stars laugh at such idiocy

00:23:42.450 --> 00:23:52.410
Subtitled by:
Central Anime(Kansas)

00:24:02.000 --> 00:24:16.000
A long relationship, that is just like the character "humans"

00:24:17.000 --> 00:24:23.200
They love and support...

00:24:24.150 --> 00:24:30.550
...while at the same time pursuing their own dreams

00:24:30.550 --> 00:24:35.700
And I feel that's okay

00:24:53.620 --> 00:24:58.520
Preview of Next Episode

00:24:54.840 --> 00:24:59.190
In March of Imperial Year 485,
Reinhard, who had become a Commodore...

00:24:59.190 --> 00:25:03.030
...was at Vanfleet{Banfried} Starzone,
leading a fleet of over 100 ships.

00:25:03.030 --> 00:25:06.620
Only a Commodore, he couldn't exercise
enough power to play a major role...

00:25:06.620 --> 00:25:10.530
...in deciding the outcome of the
battles, and he grows frustrated, but...

00:25:10.530 --> 00:25:12.950
Next episode of Legend of
Galactic Heroes Gaiden...

00:25:13.600 --> 00:25:23.650
Legend of the Galactic Heroes Gaiden
Chapter 1

00:25:13.600 --> 00:25:23.650
A Hundred Billion Stars,
a Hundred Billion Lights -
The Battle of Van-Fleet{Banfried} Starzone.

00:25:19.550 --> 00:25:22.620
Men's ambitions run through the galaxy.
